+---
+id: task-002-record-createdat-and-updatedat-on-tasks
+type: task
+title: "Record createdAt and updatedAt on tasks"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Record createdAt and updatedAt on tasks
+
+## Request
+
+The app should show how old a task is and what changed recently. Record when each task was created
+and when it was last changed.
+
+- Every task has `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, ISO-8601 date-time strings.
+- When a task is added, the two are the same.
+- Every change to a task (completing, reopening, renaming, tagging or untagging it) sets its
+  `updatedAt` to the time of the change.
+
+## Traceability
+
+- Feature: task list for the Tidy Tasks app (`README.md`).
+- Requirement: a task records when it was created and when it was last changed.
+- Acceptance: see the request above; covered by tests in `test/list.test.ts`.
+
+## Design
+
+- `Task` gets readonly `createdAt` and `updatedAt` strings. `createTask` takes the time of creation
+  and sets both fields to it.
+- The domain does not read the clock (directive r3). The time reaches the domain as a value: the
+  list is built with a clock, `createTaskList(clock)`, and each change passes `clock()` down to the
+  task function that makes it. The clock is read only at the edge, in `createTodoList` in
+  `src/index.ts`, which defaults to `new Date().toISOString()` and may be given another clock.
+- A change that leaves the task as it was (a tag it already has, an untag of a tag it lacks, a rename
+  to its current title) is not a change, so `updatedAt` stays as it was.
+- `remove` and `get` do not touch timestamps.
+
+## Notes
+
+- No credentials or secrets are involved.
+- Public API change: `Task` gains `createdAt` and `updatedAt`; `createTodoList` takes an optional
+  clock. Additive for existing callers.
